# The player's netnavi. 32x48, soles on row 47, drawn at 2x.
#
# Every coloured pixel is cyan, because in a 3x3 duel hue is the only thing the
# player has time to parse (see the palette header). The chrome is structural —
# helmet rim, belt, boots — and deliberately never tinted, so it reads as
# equipment rather than as a second team colour.
#
# Horizontally symmetric, which per STYLE.md is what keeps a mirrored frame
# legal if this ever gains a walk cycle.
name battlegrid-navi
size 32 48
key o outline
key d cyan-0-shadow
key c cyan-1
key C cyan-2
key H cyan-3-hilite
key k chrome-1
key M chrome-3-hilite
pixels
................................
...............oo...............
..............oHHo..............
.............oHHHHo.............
..........ooooHHHHoooo..........
........occCCCCCCCCCCcco........
*2 ........oCCCCCCCCCCCCCCo........
........oCooooooooooooCo........
........oCokkkkkkkkkkoCo........
........oCokkkHHHHkkkoCo........
........oCokkkkkkkkkkoCo........
........oCooooooooooooCo........
........oCCCCCCCCCCCCCCo........
........occCCCCCCCCCCcco........
..........okMMMMMMMMko..........
.....ooooCCCCCCCCCCCCCCoooo.....
*2 ....oCCCCccccccccccccccCCCCo....
....oddCCccccccccccccccCCddo....
....oooCCccccccccccccccCCooo....
......occcccccccccccccccco......
......occcccccHHHHccccccco......
*2 ......occccccHHHHHHcccccco......
......occcccccHHHHccccccco......
*2 ......occcccccccccccccccco......
......oddddddddddddddddddo......
......okkkkkkkkkkkkkkkkkko......
......oddddddddddddddddddo......
*2 .......occcccccccccccccco.......
*10 ........occccco..occccco........
*4 ........okMMMko..okMMMko........
........ooooooo..ooooooo........
